WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.487 --> 00:00:01.904
- Irish is a different language?

00:00:01.904 --> 00:00:06.904
(bouncy music)

00:00:07.105 --> 00:00:08.591
- [Voiceover] Tigh.

00:00:08.591 --> 00:00:09.798
- Whaaaat?

00:00:09.798 --> 00:00:11.586
- Who could forget a tadgch?

00:00:11.586 --> 00:00:12.468
- Taig.

00:00:12.468 --> 00:00:13.653
- Tad-g-h?

00:00:13.653 --> 00:00:14.535
- Tag.

00:00:14.535 --> 00:00:15.185
- Tod.

00:00:15.185 --> 00:00:16.044
- Tig?

00:00:16.044 --> 00:00:17.786
- [Voiceover] Yeah, like
the first syllable of tiger.

00:00:17.786 --> 00:00:18.993
- Ohhhhhhh.

00:00:18.993 --> 00:00:20.577
- I didn't see that coming.

00:00:20.577 --> 00:00:22.002
- [Voiceover] Rosheen.

00:00:22.002 --> 00:00:25.866
- Uh-oh. We got one of those weird symbols

00:00:25.866 --> 00:00:27.677
that I never knew what to do with.

00:00:27.677 --> 00:00:31.740
- In a way that you
wouldn't expect, raisin.

00:00:31.740 --> 00:00:32.808
- Reesewin.

00:00:32.808 --> 00:00:33.783
- Roisin.

00:00:33.783 --> 00:00:34.480
- Rozeen.

00:00:34.480 --> 00:00:35.153
- Rizin.

00:00:35.153 --> 00:00:36.152
- [Voiceover] It's Rosheen.

00:00:36.152 --> 00:00:36.802
(snorts)

00:00:36.802 --> 00:00:39.718
- Rosheeeeen. So what does that symbol do?

00:00:39.718 --> 00:00:41.330
- [Voiceover] Sersha.

00:00:41.330 --> 00:00:43.326
- This one I should know because

00:00:43.326 --> 00:00:45.509
there's an actress that has this name,

00:00:45.509 --> 00:00:47.134
and she was in a Wes Anderson movie.

00:00:47.134 --> 00:00:49.781
- These combination of
letters is just so strange.

00:00:49.781 --> 00:00:50.803
- Shar-say.

00:00:50.803 --> 00:00:51.662
- Sarosee.

00:00:51.662 --> 00:00:52.777
- Swearzee.

00:00:52.777 --> 00:00:53.729
- Sweersha?

00:00:53.729 --> 00:00:56.598
- Sersha? These are really pretty names,

00:00:56.598 --> 00:00:58.628
but I, they're spelled so weird.

00:00:58.628 --> 00:00:59.998
- [Voiceover] Kiva.

00:00:59.998 --> 00:01:02.645
- Guys, you tell me what
you do with an m and an h,

00:01:02.645 --> 00:01:03.968
cause I'm at a loss.

00:01:03.968 --> 00:01:05.292
- This looks like Portuguese.

00:01:05.292 --> 00:01:06.360
- Cha-mee.

00:01:06.360 --> 00:01:07.497
- Comehee.

00:01:07.497 --> 00:01:10.400
- Maybe it's just simple,
maybe it's just Cowmee.

00:01:10.400 --> 00:01:11.758
- Come-hee?

00:01:11.758 --> 00:01:14.138
- Kiva? I'm sorry, what?

00:01:14.138 --> 00:01:15.136
There's a v in there?

00:01:15.136 --> 00:01:17.542
- [Voiceover] Owen.

00:01:17.542 --> 00:01:19.780
- Some of these letters
are not being used.

00:01:19.780 --> 00:01:21.824
It's just me figuring out which ones.

00:01:21.824 --> 00:01:23.356
- Egan. Totally Egan.

00:01:23.356 --> 00:01:24.262
- Uh, Johan.

00:01:24.262 --> 00:01:25.190
- Eogan.

00:01:25.190 --> 00:01:25.794
- Ethan.

00:01:25.794 --> 00:01:26.398
- Eugan.

00:01:26.398 --> 00:01:27.104
- I give up.

00:01:27.104 --> 00:01:27.878
- [Voiceover] Owen.

00:01:27.878 --> 00:01:30.275
- Owen? No.

00:01:30.275 --> 00:01:33.271
- Why is a e in there
if it has no purpose?

00:01:33.271 --> 00:01:35.523
If there's no e in
Owen, oh, yeah there is.

00:01:35.523 --> 00:01:36.335
Never mind.

00:01:36.335 --> 00:01:37.926
- [Voiceover] Maraid.

00:01:37.926 --> 00:01:40.265
- I don't know what the
little thing is above the e.

00:01:40.265 --> 00:01:41.606
- [Voiceover] It's called a fada.

00:01:41.606 --> 00:01:42.535
- Maired.

00:01:42.535 --> 00:01:43.603
- Maeread.

00:01:43.603 --> 00:01:46.529
- So I think it would be Mairead, but

00:01:46.529 --> 00:01:48.340
it's probably like Vaired.

00:01:48.340 --> 00:01:49.083
- Merd.

00:01:49.083 --> 00:01:50.011
- Mary.

00:01:50.011 --> 00:01:51.219
- Maraid?

00:01:51.219 --> 00:01:54.075
What is that, it's like a,
it's like a male parade.

00:01:54.075 --> 00:01:57.581
- I don't even know what a's are anymore.

00:01:57.581 --> 00:01:59.113
- [Voiceover] Neiff.

00:01:59.113 --> 00:02:01.412
- This name is just Name.

00:02:01.412 --> 00:02:03.107
- Naame. Niama?

00:02:03.107 --> 00:02:05.127
- Niam-hee. Naomi!

00:02:05.127 --> 00:02:06.033
- Neeam.

00:02:06.033 --> 00:02:07.611
- Like Liam, but it's an n?

00:02:07.611 --> 00:02:08.772
- Niam.

00:02:08.772 --> 00:02:11.326
- Nimh. Like, uh, the mice.

00:02:11.326 --> 00:02:13.881
- Nieff? I'm sorry, what?

00:02:13.881 --> 00:02:16.249
I am not getting that from this.

00:02:16.249 --> 00:02:17.805
- [Voiceover] Granya.

00:02:17.805 --> 00:02:19.941
- This is a term of endearment
for your grandmother.

00:02:19.941 --> 00:02:20.707
- Granny.

00:02:20.707 --> 00:02:22.216
- I don't know how else to pronounce it

00:02:22.216 --> 00:02:23.145
other than Grainy.

00:02:23.145 --> 00:02:24.770
- Gra-Graenee.

00:02:24.770 --> 00:02:26.303
- Gra-Grainee.

00:02:26.303 --> 00:02:28.903
- There's literally no
other way to say this.

00:02:28.903 --> 00:02:31.364
And if they say it a
different way, it's wrong.

00:02:31.364 --> 00:02:32.363
It's Grain.

00:02:32.363 --> 00:02:33.524
- What is it?

00:02:33.524 --> 00:02:34.604
- [Voiceover] Granya.

00:02:34.604 --> 00:02:35.892
- Granya.

00:02:35.892 --> 00:02:37.053
- That's beautiful.

00:02:37.053 --> 00:02:38.423
- I feel like they can make a big comeback

00:02:38.423 --> 00:02:40.513
in like a hipster way.

00:02:40.513 --> 00:02:43.438
Which, the Irish better watch out.

00:02:43.438 --> 00:02:44.205
- [Voiceover] That's not to say

00:02:44.205 --> 00:02:46.318
that Irish names are confusing.

00:02:46.318 --> 00:02:48.779
I just find language confusing.

00:02:48.779 --> 00:02:52.779
- I can barely speak English.

